"t":"If r is a differentiable vector function of t of constant length, then"},{"x":0.62109,"y":0.69305,"w":0.03363,"h":0.02238,"fs":0.01918,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"r # dr"},{"x":0.64066,"y":0.70136,"w":0.2806,"h":0.02074,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"dt = 0. (4)"},{"x":0.08775,"y":0.71213,"w":0.23799,"h":0.04297,"fs":0.01151,"n":4,"k":1,"t":"FIGURE 13.8 If a particle moves on a sphere in such a way that its position r is a differentiable function of time, then"},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.74726,"w":0.59297,"h":0.02814,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"We will use this observation repeatedly in Section 13.4. The converse is also true (see Exercise 27)."},{"x":0.08857,"y":0.74955,"w":0.09229,"h":0.02144,"fs":0.01727,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"r # (dr>dt) = 0."},{"x":0.08618,"y":0.81055,"w":0.17484,"h":0.02814,"fs":0.02814,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"Exercises 13.1"},{"x":0.54712,"y":0.84731,"w":0.13261,"h":0.02498,"fs":0.01151,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"2. r(t) = t t + 1 i + 1"},{"x":0.67399,"y":0.84749,"w":0.07809,"h":0.02332,"fs":0.01151,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"t j, t = - 1"},{"x":0.08824,"y":0.84907,"w":0.41593,"h":0.06829,"fs":0.01151,"n":5,"k":1,"t":"Motion in the Plane In Exercises 1–4, r(t) is the position of a particle in the xy-plane at time t. Find an equation in x and y whose graph is the path of the par- ticle. Then find the particle’s velocity and acceleration vectors at the given value of t."},{"x":0.54711,"y":0.8833,"w":0.195,"h":0.0248,"fs":0.01151,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"3. r(t) = eti + 2 9e2tj, t = ln 3"},{"x":0.0956,"y":0.91911,"w":0.24015,"h":0.01643,"fs":0.01261,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"1. r(t) = (t + 1)i + (t2 - 1)j, t = 1"},{"x":0.54711,"y":0.92124,"w":0.24033,"h":0.01212,"fs":0.01151,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"4. r(t) = (cos 2t)i + (3sin 2t)j, t = 0"}]}